{
  "id": "enm_001",
  "category": "enumerative",
  "severity": "MEDIUM",
  "question": "List every requirement related to doors in UN R95.",
  "answer": "The doors shall be closed, but not locked. [UN-ECE-R95 §Annex 4, p.24]\n\nAfter the impact, the side doors on the non-struck side shall be unlocked. [UN-ECE-R95 §5, p.10]\n\nIn the case of vehicles equipped with an automatically activated door locking system, the doors shall be locked before the moment of impact and be unlocked after the impact at least on the non-struck side. [UN-ECE-R95 §5, p.10]\n\nThe space for occupant accommodation, bounded by the roof, floor, side walls, doors, outside glazing, front bulkhead and rear bulkhead, or rear gate, as well as by the electrical protection barriers and enclosures provided for protecting the occupants from direct contact with high voltage live parts, is considered the passenger compartment for electric safety assessment. [UN-ECE-R95 §2, p.6]\n\nThe passenger compartment means the space for occupant accommodation, bounded by the roof, floor, side walls, doors, outside glazing and front bulkhead and the plane of the rear compartment bulkhead or the plane of the rear-seat back support. [UN-ECE-R95 §2, p.5]",
